  "body": "Conversation submissions and projections need durable recovery and owner-bound responses across reloads, authentication changes, and delayed requests. This branch adds journal/reconciliation handling, session acknowledgement checks, projection freshness regressions, and browser scenarios. It also strengthens source/proof observations, fixes nested fixture custody, and validates ownership of the browser-test server on its exact port.\n\nThis is a draft engineering proposal. At head `b64fdad2`, the retained local required attempt was refused for Git metadata identity drift and canceled before test selection or execution. That attempt supplies no passing-test credit. Fresh exact-head required execution, hosted checks, and independent review remain necessary before merge. No installed-service, authenticated-provider, or release qualification is claimed.\n",
